A||||4||Fret Naught||Head Light to Ashtray||||5||
Z||000000||Fret Naught||09-09-2000||02:34 PM||||Got a question,<BR>As some of you know, I had my hood painted at the begining of summer, and it sucked, so I finally took it back and they re painted, this time, they took the hood off and stripped it. I have had it for about a week now, and last night when it came time to flip on the head lights, one of them would not open. I got out, and inspected, it is trying to open, but hanging up on a piece of plastic on the inside. When I give it a pull it pops up. I am not taking it back, and before I jump in and start messing with it, I was wondering if there is some kide of alignment screws or proceedure?<P>Ashtrays, they won't stay closed just flop open. I had the console apart awhile back, and did not see any springs or clips that I would have expected to see, designed to hold the lids closed/open. Any suggestions?<P>Any way, thanks in advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-09-2000||05:01 PM||||Ok, couple of things about the headlights.<BR>They couldve either a.) mis-aligned the hood..it dosnt take much, the bolts on the front of the car attaching the hood need to be marked before taking the hood off...check around to see if the hood looks lot be aligned right....or b.) they took the headlight covers off and also mis-aligned those. There are two 10mm bolts (I believe) that take off each cover. I had this prob while putting a new hood on one of my Fieros. Easy fix.<BR>The ashtray lids each have a metal "moonshape" clip on them. This keeps them closed. They are held on by a plastic piece that more times than not breaks when you try to take them off. Once again, pretty easy fix.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||09-11-2000||01:26 AM||||Well I checked to see what was happening, and it looks like when they put the hood back on, they did not mark the hinges!!!! So, I losened them up a bit and slid it forward a skosh. Now the head lights open, but the lines look really crappy!! if anybody has a proceedure for aligning the hood on the hinges so that the fender and fronts gaps look good it would be much appreciated.<BR>Thanks again||||reg||11
Z||000003||mrfiero||09-11-2000||01:40 AM||||The ashtray doors have a small "moon" shaped spring thing to keep them from flopping open (that's really annoying, isn't it?).<P>I can send you a pair of these springs if you want.  You need to be very careful putting them on though....those doors tend to snap easily.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Fret Naught||09-12-2000||03:09 PM||||Thanks MRFiero, I might take you up on the clips, I will see what I can come up with locally first though.<P>To all others, I could sure use some direction on how to line up my hood, there must be a set proceedure somewhere||||reg||7
